## Status

State honestly what has been *booted* versus merely *built*. A reader who knows
which parts are load-bearing can work around gaps; one who finds out by hitting
them cannot.

| Machine | SoC | State |
|---|---|---|
| `<machine>` | <soc> | builds, boots on hardware |
| `<machine>` | <soc> | **build-only -- never booted** |

## Quick start

> Every command below has been run in order, on a clean machine, by someone who
> is not the author. If you change them, do that again.

```sh
# 1. Host tooling (once).
<...>

# 2. Point the build somewhere with 100+ GiB free.
export KAS_WORK_DIR=/path/with/space/<product>-build
export KAS_CONTAINER_ENGINE=docker

# 3. Build.
uv run kas-container build kas/machine/<board>.yml:kas/variant/debug.yml

# 4. Flash.
<...>
```

Console: **<baud> 8N1 on `<tty>`**. See [FLASHING.md](docs/FLASHING.md).

## Repository layout

```
kas/                  the ONLY place repos and pins are declared
  machine/*.yml       one fragment per board
  variant/*.yml       debug vs release; local.conf overlays only
meta-<vendor>-bsp/    reusable: machine confs, SoC-agnostic mechanisms
meta-<product>/       distro, images, application recipes
patches/              patches against upstream layers; never edit in place
docs/                 see below
```

## Requirements

| Requirement | Notes |
|---|---|
| Docker | running, user in the `docker` group |
| `uv` | installs the exact pinned `kas` |
| Disk | **100+ GiB free**; the most common way a first build fails |
| RAM | 16 GiB minimum |
| First build | <N> hours. Budget a day. |

